The mesh keeps the source's native frame -- x = the ~99 mm long bar the lenses are arrayed across,
y = height ~23 mm, z = depth ~20 mm with +z the lens face's outward normal -- the same convention as
the d435 and d455 meshes, so no reorientation was applied.

Every pose in roqsim_sensors/models/realsense_d415/realsense_d415.xml and in the `frames:` block of
realsense_d415.manifest.yaml -- the mesh in camera_link, the `d415_color` camera at the colour
optical frame, the depth frames -- is read from the same repository's
realsense2_description/urdf/_d415.urdf.xacro by external/convert/build_realsense_devices.py, not
measured off the mesh. The camera's `fovy` is the D415 colour vertical FOV from the datasheet.
